<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Adelin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1103–1120</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Adelin was the only legitimate son of Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Matilda of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, and heir to England and Normandy. He received the homage of the Norman barons and in 1120 did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france">Louis VI of France</a> for the duchy. On 25 November 1120 he drowned when the White Ship sank off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barfleur">Barfleur</a>, leaving Henry without a male heir and opening the way to the civil war known as the Anarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-adelin.jpg" alt="William Adelin" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vil%C3%A9m_syn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
